cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "eyelogic-recorder: asynchronous recording for EyeLogic eye trackers in Python"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-21"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23537087"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/laubrock-lab/eyelogic-recorder"
authors:
  - family-names: Laubrock
    given-names: Jochen
    affiliation: University of Potsdam
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0798-8977"
abstract: >-
  A lightweight Python client for EyeLogic eye trackers, built on the official
  EyeLogic SDK. It records every gaze sample asynchronously to plain CSV without
  ever blocking the SDK callback, writes timestamped messages on the same clock,
  reports errors as typed exceptions, and includes a simulated tracker, PsychoPy
  example experiments (boundary paradigm, moving window, paragraph reading,
  free viewing) and benchmarks.
keywords:
  - eye tracking
  - EyeLogic
  - PsychoPy
  - reading
  - gaze-contingent display
  - data recording
